162:| C3 feature collapse causes size 100 | Rejected as necessary cause | `Psi_hat=0` still gives 10/10 size 100 |
163:| Learned C3 is healthy/irrelevant numerically | Rejected | epoch-200 grand `Psi` error is +2646.997 on average |
164:| Learned singleton path drives the symptom | Supported | zero-C3 C1+C2 argmax is size 100 in 10/10 |
170:| C3 target contains learned singleton error | Rejected | singleton outcomes used in the label are exact evaluator outcomes |
9:Measured **20 real anchors** from `V025_PROBE/world/3` in pilot evaluation order (step, then the three sealed reference carriers), with 4 final epoch-2000 FULL lineages: **80 matched anchor-seed decisions**. The selector inputs and catalogue are the pilot's deployed `_build_anchor_rows(..., full_legal_actions=True)` and `_catalogue_with_census` paths. Exact Ψ is from `_exact_interactions` on every legal row; learned Ψ is `model.interaction(context)` with the production `contexts.get(configuration_id)` gate. Every comparison removes only the interaction term from the same FULL model's scores and applies score-descending / lexicographic-configuration-ID argmax.
